==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈmaːðʏr]|lang=is}}
*: {{audio|Is-maður.ogg|Audio (Iceland, Kópavogur)}}
*: {{rhymes|aːðʏr|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|maðr}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|g=BALDUR|manns|menn}}

# [[man]], [[human being]]
#* ''[[það|Það]] [[tilheyra|tilheyrir]] [[náttúra|náttúru]] '''mannsins''' [[hata|að hata]] [[þeir|þá]] [[sem]] [[hann]] [[hafa|hefur]] [[særa|sært]].''
#*: It belongs to '''human''' [[nature]] [[hate|to hate]] those that he has [[injure]]d.
# [[husband]] (most often used with {{definite}} article)
#* ''[[þetta|Þetta]] er [[Geir]], '''maðurinn''' [[minn]].''
#*: This is Geir, [[my]] '''husband'''.
# [[chessman]]
#* ''[[færa|Færðu]] '''manninn''' [[þinn]].''
#*: [[move|Move]] [[your]] '''chessman'''.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-maður|}}

